Passage: DIR, Annex I, 1.1.1

[0] 1.1.1.
[1] Definitions For the purpose of this Annex:
[2] (a) ‘hazard’ means a potential source of injury or damage to health;
[3] (b) ‘danger zone’ means any zone within and/or around machinery in which a person is subject to a risk to his health or safety;
[4] (c) ‘exposed person’ means any person wholly or partially in a danger zone;
[5] (d) ‘operator’ means the person or persons installing, operating, adjusting, maintaining, cleaning, repairing or moving machinery;
[6] (e) ‘risk’ means a combination of the probability and the degree of an injury or damage to health that can arise in a hazardous situation;
[7] (f) ‘guard’ means a part of the machinery used specifically to provide protection by means of a physical barrier;
[8] (g) ‘protective device’ means a device (other than a guard) which reduces the risk, either alone or in conjunction with a guard;
[9] (h) ‘intended use’ means the use of machinery in accordance with the information provided in the instructions for use;
[10] (i) ‘reasonably foreseeable misuse’ means the use of machinery in a way not intended in the instructions for use, but which may result from readily predictable human behaviour.
